  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Suppose that \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) are nonzero real numbers such that\n\n\\[\\frac{3x + y}{x - 3y} = -2.\\]\n\nWhat is the value of \\[\\frac{x + 3y}{3x - y}?\\]",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(3\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": "2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2017-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The equation gives \\(3x + y = -2(x - 3y)\\) \\(= -2x + 6y,\\) so \\(5x = 5y,\\) meaning \\(x = y.\\) Then \\[\\frac{x + 3y}{3x - y} = \\frac{y + 3y}{3y - y} = \\frac{4y}{2y} = 2.\\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Clear the denominator: \\(3x + y = -2(x - 3y)\\)",
        "This simplifies to \\(x = y;\\) substitute into the target expression"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
